<title>USA: Union reaches pact with five supermarket chains.</title>
<headline>Union reaches pact with five supermarket chains.</headline>
<dateline>WOODBRIDGE, N.J. 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Local 1262 of the United Food and Commercial Workers Union said Monday that it has reached a tentative agreement with five supermarket chains on a new contract for 28,000 employees in 288 stores.</p>
<p>The chains are Koninklijke Ahold NV's Edwards Super Food Stores, Grand Union Co, Foodtown, Pathmark and ShopRite.</p>
<p>The union said that full details of the agreement will be given to union members in a series of meetings scheduled over the next two weeks and that the membership must then vote to accept or reject the proposed contract.</p>
</text>
